      "nodes": [
        {
          "t": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What It Means to be Nearsighted",
          "html": "What It Means to be Nearsighted&nbsp;",
          "align": "center",
          "id": "sUw6aGfT1W",
          "col": 0,
          "origin": "static"
        },
        {
          "t": "html",
          "html": "<p>Myopia means your child can see things up close, but distant objects, like the board at school or signs far away, start to look blurry. This happens because the eye grows longer than it should, causing light to focus in the wrong place. As kids grow, their eyes can continue to change, which is why prescriptions often keep increasing over time.</p>",
          "align": "center",
          "id": "FSImutE3WG",
          "col": 0,
          "origin": "static"
        },
        {
          "t": "button",
